WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.027
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore
Run oncotracer --interactive --backend conda. Choose New analysis or Continue an existing analysis. This is a synthetic demo.

2
00:00:05.027 --> 00:00:06.957
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · new analysis
Choose New analysis to open sample setup. Continue an existing analysis is for a saved output project.

3
00:00:06.957 --> 00:00:13.821
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · preservation
Choose preservation from specimen records. Fresh is selected only as demonstration metadata here.

4
00:00:13.821 --> 00:00:28.498
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · discover inputs
Choose fastq_pass. Each barcode stays one sample, even when it contains several FASTQ batches.

5
00:00:28.498 --> 00:00:34.060
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · sample groups
Assign the example sample to Cancer. Use the type dropdown; you can also drag cards between groups.

6
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.453
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · sample name
Rename barcode01 to DRR165691. The barcode still identifies the same FASTQ input.

7
00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:47.041
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · CNA settings
Keep Copy-number analysis, ichorCNA and 500 kb bins. FASTQs alone do not provide methylation calls.

8
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:53.667
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · tools and reference
Choose the backend you installed. Keep prepared hg38 download; real downloads begin only when you start analysis.

9
00:00:53.667 --> 00:01:00.481
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · separate project
Confirm a distinct project folder. Keep optional short-variant analysis off for this CNA QuickStart.

10
00:01:00.481 --> 00:01:07.541
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · save and review
Save configuration and check. Resolve any errors before Run analysis. These displayed checks are simulated.

11
00:01:07.541 --> 00:01:14.458
QuickStart 1 · Oxford Nanopore · ready for your run
In a real project, choose Run analysis after checks pass and keep its terminal open. This demo stops here; no analysis was run.
